(774621, 84814, 9906, '<td valign="top">Your color portion of this shot doesn''t quite look right, kinda like it''s pasted in.  Don''t know if it''s because the colors are alittle dull or because the delineation is too sharp.  Next time try feathering your selection to make the transition a touch more gradual...<br/>TC</td>', 'Your color portion of this shot doesn''t quite look right, kinda like it''s pasted in.  Don''t know if it''s because the colors are alittle dull or because the delineation is too sharp.  Next time try feathering your selection to make the transition a touch more gradual...TC', '2004-06-23 02:04:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(774631, 84644, 9906, '<td valign="top">IMHO, this is a touch too contrasty (probably the harsh light from the time of day it was taken).  Never thought I''d say that about a (mostly) b/w image.  Also (once again just my opinion) I think it would have had more oomph if you would have left the whole grader (I think that''s what the machine is) in color and not just the yellows...<br/>TC</td>', 'IMHO, this is a touch too contrasty (probably the harsh light from the time of day it was taken).  Never thought I''d say that about a (mostly) b/w image.  Also (once again just my opinion) I think it would have had more oomph if you would have left the whole grader (I think that''s what the machine is) in color and not just the yellows...TC', '2004-06-23 02:06:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(774655, 84914, 14355, '<td valign="top">This is extremely nice, but, there is some blue in the top left area not greyscalled.  So, I recalibrated my monitor and guess what?  It''s gone now.  Very nice detailed image, wonderful colors, and excellent depth of focus.</td>', 'This is extremely nice, but, there is some blue in the top left area not greyscalled.  So, I recalibrated my monitor and guess what?  It''s gone now.  Very nice detailed image, wonderful colors, and excellent depth of focus.', '2004-06-23 02:13:32.000000', NULL, 1),
