(778935, 84567, 14355, '<td valign="top">Looking at this a second time.  Too bad a larger version couldn''t have been uploaded and displayed.  That would have given the picture the impact it deserved - matted and framed it would be winner.  Probably looks nice on your monitor!</td>', 'Looking at this a second time.  Too bad a larger version couldn''t have been uploaded and displayed.  That would have given the picture the impact it deserved - matted and framed it would be winner.  Probably looks nice on your monitor!', '2004-06-25 01:27:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(778937, 84905, 14355, '<td valign="top">There is a light green tinge to the pic - and it''s tough to tell what was desaturated.</td>', 'There is a light green tinge to the pic - and it''s tough to tell what was desaturated.', '2004-06-25 01:28:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(778940, 84928, 14355, '<td valign="top">I''m sure you know how much I love this picture.  I think the flowers would have the better object to desaturate.</td>', 'I''m sure you know how much I love this picture.  I think the flowers would have the better object to desaturate.', '2004-06-25 01:31:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(778945, 84790, 14355, '<td valign="top">The more I come back to this picture - the sharp focus, great dof, and stark reality - it really is a great picture.  But it totally missed the boat for a desaturated picture.  You needed to set it up so what got desaturate was obvious to the viewer.  Had you done this on a mirror - with either the pepper or it''s reflection desaturated it would have been an awesome picture.  You have tallent - you just need to think a little more like a viewer - or have someone else give them a peek.</td>', 'The more I come back to this picture - the sharp focus, great dof, and stark reality - it really is a great picture.  But it totally missed the boat for a desaturated picture.  You needed to set it up so what got desaturate was obvious to the viewer.  Had you done this on a mirror - with either the pepper or it''s reflection desaturated it would have been an awesome picture.  You have tallent - you just need to think a little more like a viewer - or have someone else give them a peek.', '2004-06-25 01:37:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(778948, 84197, 14355, '<td valign="top">This is a wonderful high contrast picture.  I would have magnified this picture and finished the greyscaling around the ears, nose, and sides - I think that would have made the eyes stand out even more.  However, with those areas still having slight hues in them - it adds some softness, it adds to the realiism of the shot.  Most viewers will assume the cat looks like this normally!  Good picture.</td>', 'This is a wonderful high contrast picture.  I would have magnified this picture and finished the greyscaling around the ears, nose, and sides - I think that would have made the eyes stand out even more.  However, with those areas still having slight hues in them - it adds some softness, it adds to the realiism of the shot.  Most viewers will assume the cat looks like this normally!  Good picture.', '2004-06-25 01:41:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(778953, 84870, 14355, '<td valign="top">You know how much I love this picture - I had to come back!  LOL  The crop is a bit tight - looser and with something else in the background close to focus would have made a better composition.  The flowers colors look un-natural, as if some colors in the flower were lost during the desat process.  Excellent workmanship separating the flower from the background.  I think if you had a friend look this over before you submitted it - you''d have picked up on thes points.  I always let someone else pick the best one for me.</td>', 'You know how much I love this picture - I had to come back!  LOL  The crop is a bit tight - looser and with something else in the background close to focus would have made a better composition.  The flowers colors look un-natural, as if some colors in the flower were lost during the desat process.  Excellent workmanship separating the flower from the background.  I think if you had a friend look this over before you submitted it - you''d have picked up on thes points.  I always let someone else pick the best one for me.', '2004-06-25 01:47:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(778957, 84796, 14355, '<td valign="top">Backgound is sepia and not greyscaled as mentioned in the challenge.  One tree might look fine, but, with all the rest it looks very much like a normal picture taken on a cloudy day.</td>', 'Backgound is sepia and not greyscaled as mentioned in the challenge.  One tree might look fine, but, with all the rest it looks very much like a normal picture taken on a cloudy day.', '2004-06-25 01:49:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(778965, 84613, 14355, '<td valign="top">This is a really cool picture - great colors, focus, and effects.  But too many colors all over the shot for me to consider this a desaturated picture.  If the purple aspects were greyscalled it would have been a winner........ probably wouldn''t have looked as nice as it does now, but, it would have ''fit'' the challenge better.  Small sacrifice to pay for winning.  Frammed and matted - this picture would sell.</td>', 'This is a really cool picture - great colors, focus, and effects.  But too many colors all over the shot for me to consider this a desaturated picture.  If the purple aspects were greyscalled it would have been a winner........ probably wouldn''t have looked as nice as it does now, but, it would have ''fit'' the challenge better.  Small sacrifice to pay for winning.  Frammed and matted - this picture would sell.', '2004-06-25 01:53:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(778968, 84323, 14355, '<td valign="top">Not the best choice in picture to use - there is no real subject. The car is a deffinite detractor - with it copped out the picture would have been much better because you have excellent contrast between the flags and background.  That, and leaving the stream in color to ''anchor'' the shot for balance after cropping the vehicle would have put this one in the running for top place.</td>', 'Not the best choice in picture to use - there is no real subject. The car is a deffinite detractor - with it copped out the picture would have been much better because you have excellent contrast between the flags and background.  That, and leaving the stream in color to ''anchor'' the shot for balance after cropping the vehicle would have put this one in the running for top place.', '2004-06-25 01:58:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(778974, 84787, 14355, '<td valign="top">Threre are waaaaaaay too many things that missed desaturation.  I would have left one or two similar items left color - not this much. The picture has excellent contrast.  You certainly started with a great picture - if it had one item or a small set of items standing out I would have voted it fairly high.</td>', 'Threre are waaaaaaay too many things that missed desaturation.  I would have left one or two similar items left color - not this much. The picture has excellent contrast.  You certainly started with a great picture - if it had one item or a small set of items standing out I would have voted it fairly high.', '2004-06-25 02:01:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(778988, 84474, 14355, '<td valign="top">Nice try - and a good high contrast picture to use.  Looks to me that the greens and blues on desaturation removed some of the hues that make the red look real.  This looks like a black and white picture with a pure red icon drawn on it - and you very seldom find a pure red anywhere - except in some roses.</td>', 'Nice try - and a good high contrast picture to use.  Looks to me that the greens and blues on desaturation removed some of the hues that make the red look real.  This looks like a black and white picture with a pure red icon drawn on it - and you very seldom find a pure red anywhere - except in some roses.', '2004-06-25 02:11:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(778995, 84357, 14355, '<td valign="top">This picture has a bad angle - it''s the wrong side of a bird for a good portrait!  The crop is way too tight - some of the tail feathers on the left are clipped - and there is no balance for the negative space on the right.</td>', 'This picture has a bad angle - it''s the wrong side of a bird for a good portrait!  The crop is way too tight - some of the tail feathers on the left are clipped - and there is no balance for the negative space on the right.', '2004-06-25 02:15:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(778999, 84913, 14355, '<td valign="top">You know how much I love this picture.  In color it''s probably grand.  But when reduced to greyscale all the magic of the greens disapear and the entire forground turns into negative space.   I would have cropped the whole bottom half off and displayed it as a rectangle crop.  Then colored one green tree on the far left to balance the shot between sky and barn.  You were on the right track, but, I''m guessing your mind was still thinking in ''color'' when working on the picture.</td>', 'You know how much I love this picture.  In color it''s probably grand.  But when reduced to greyscale all the magic of the greens disapear and the entire forground turns into negative space.   I would have cropped the whole bottom half off and displayed it as a rectangle crop.  Then colored one green tree on the far left to balance the shot between sky and barn.  You were on the right track, but, I''m guessing your mind was still thinking in ''color'' when working on the picture.', '2004-06-25 02:20:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(779002, 84621, 14355, '<td valign="top">Not a great picture to use for this challenge - spiders give many people the creeps, especially when macro''s in this close..  Crop is a little too tight - would have been nice to have something else in near focus pictures with it.  The subject is confusing - one nice and bright, the other (spider) not.  Great workmanship isolating the flower from the background, and, you desaturated the picture without effecting the flower.  Nice job overall.</td>', 'Not a great picture to use for this challenge - spiders give many people the creeps, especially when macro''s in this close..  Crop is a little too tight - would have been nice to have something else in near focus pictures with it.  The subject is confusing - one nice and bright, the other (spider) not.  Great workmanship isolating the flower from the background, and, you desaturated the picture without effecting the flower.  Nice job overall.', '2004-06-25 02:24:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(779006, 84809, 14355, '<td valign="top">It''s a good high contrast picture - and the desaturation is fine - but it''s not composed well.  No subject, theme, or interest.</td>', 'It''s a good high contrast picture - and the desaturation is fine - but it''s not composed well.  No subject, theme, or interest.', '2004-06-25 02:27:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(779007, 84906, 17551, '<td valign="top">I like this. something different that I admire.</td>', 'I like this. something different that I admire.', '2004-06-25 02:28:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(779009, 84556, 17551, '<td valign="top">Great shot, and the desaturation works very well here. I think this will be top 10</td>', 'Great shot, and the desaturation works very well here. I think this will be top 10', '2004-06-25 02:28:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(779012, 84888, 14355, '<td valign="top">This is an awesome picture.  I ike every aspect of it - and a nice surprise seeing the little lizard yellow and not green.  You should sell this to your local cell phone company!</td>', 'This is an awesome picture.  I ike every aspect of it - and a nice surprise seeing the little lizard yellow and not green.  You should sell this to your local cell phone company!', '2004-06-25 02:31:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(779013, 84424, 17551, '<td valign="top">I love your choice of subject, but there are a couple of things that I would change about the shot (but only for this challenge). I think its a little too tight on the subject, and it seems to fill the frame and lessons the effect of desaturation.. The other thing to change is maybe the hue (or the title), as it looks more orange to me =). good luck!</td>', 'I love your choice of subject, but there are a couple of things that I would change about the shot (but only for this challenge). I think its a little too tight on the subject, and it seems to fill the frame and lessons the effect of desaturation.. The other thing to change is maybe the hue (or the title), as it looks more orange to me =). good luck!', '2004-06-25 02:32:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(779014, 84774, 14355, '<td valign="top">Desaturating a whole bunch of white foam leaves you with ......... a whole bunch of white looking foam.  The desaturation effect isn''t very obvious.</td>', 'Desaturating a whole bunch of white foam leaves you with ......... a whole bunch of white looking foam.  The desaturation effect isn''t very obvious.', '2004-06-25 02:32:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(779018, 84878, 17551, '<td valign="top">awesome shot, cant wait to see what this is. 9</td>', 'awesome shot, cant wait to see what this is. 9', '2004-06-25 02:35:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(779020, 84854, 17551, '<td valign="top">lol, go the drool. I like the reverse style desat, works well for this.</td>', 'lol, go the drool. I like the reverse style desat, works well for this.', '2004-06-25 02:37:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(779024, 84383, 17551, '<td valign="top">I like it, but I''m not too fussed on the angle.. I dont know why! If it could move over to the right a little..</td>', 'I like it, but I''m not too fussed on the angle.. I dont know why! If it could move over to the right a little..', '2004-06-25 02:39:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(779025, 84911, 14355, '<td valign="top">You know how much I love this picture. The first issue is the red part of the pendent is an un indentible object.  The workmanship separating the item from the background is excellent.  What''s missing in this picture is balance and  the viewer has no idea what colors are missing - perhaps the wood always looks this way.  I would have left part of the wood inlay on top in color or the inlays on the drawers in color.</td>', 'You know how much I love this picture. The first issue is the red part of the pendent is an un indentible object.  The workmanship separating the item from the background is excellent.  What''s missing in this picture is balance and  the viewer has no idea what colors are missing - perhaps the wood always looks this way.  I would have left part of the wood inlay on top in color or the inlays on the drawers in color.', '2004-06-25 02:39:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(779033, 84783, 14355, '<td valign="top">Nice of picture of your horse, great focus, dof, and colors - just not a wise choice in picture to choose for this challenge.  The horse is already the highlight of the pic and occupies a large percentage of the picture - removing the  small amount of background doesn''t have an effect on the subject . If I had t work with this picture - I would have desaturated the entire thing except for the little bit of mane on the head and right side just below the eye.  Maybe leave the halter in color for balance.  You had great workmanship isolating the horse from the rest of the picture.</td>', 'Nice of picture of your horse, great focus, dof, and colors - just not a wise choice in picture to choose for this challenge.  The horse is already the highlight of the pic and occupies a large percentage of the picture - removing the  small amount of background doesn''t have an effect on the subject . If I had t work with this picture - I would have desaturated the entire thing except for the little bit of mane on the head and right side just below the eye.  Maybe leave the halter in color for balance.  You had great workmanship isolating the horse from the rest of the picture.', '2004-06-25 02:47:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(779038, 84800, 14355, '<td valign="top">A damn nice shot with everything you would ever want - great focus, great dof, great colors - and action.  However, when you have a white and grey bird, with black rocks, and lots of white refection on the water and greyscale it - it still looks like a normal picture when shown to someone that doesn''t know it''s been desaturated.   had you gone for a really close crop of just the bird''s head and his lunch it may have worked fine.</td>', 'A damn nice shot with everything you would ever want - great focus, great dof, great colors - and action.  However, when you have a white and grey bird, with black rocks, and lots of white refection on the water and greyscale it - it still looks like a normal picture when shown to someone that doesn''t know it''s been desaturated.   had you gone for a really close crop of just the bird''s head and his lunch it may have worked fine.', '2004-06-25 02:51:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(779041, 84819, 14355, '<td valign="top">Waaaaaaaaay too many overpowering colors in the picture because the leaves are too light and lack contrast.  You could have adjusted that in PS several ways - only downside to that is the more you dink with a picture in PS the more un-natural it tends to look.  As it looks now -  I think it would have looked great with just one berry in color.</td>', 'Waaaaaaaaay too many overpowering colors in the picture because the leaves are too light and lack contrast.  You could have adjusted that in PS several ways - only downside to that is the more you dink with a picture in PS the more un-natural it tends to look.  As it looks now -  I think it would have looked great with just one berry in color.', '2004-06-25 02:57:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(779046, 84836, 14355, '<td valign="top">The picture has great focus, a really good subject  and good dof.  Problem is the crop is so tight it automatically makes this person the main subject.  Desaturating the backgound doesn''t enhance his main role in the picture.  in a wider angle shot the effect would have been spectacular.</td>', 'The picture has great focus, a really good subject  and good dof.  Problem is the crop is so tight it automatically makes this person the main subject.  Desaturating the backgound doesn''t enhance his main role in the picture.  in a wider angle shot the effect would have been spectacular.', '2004-06-25 03:02:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(779049, 83916, 14355, '<td valign="top">This looks like a normal picture of a glass sitting on driftwood.  This happens because the viewer has no reference point on what the material is or background was.</td>', 'This looks like a normal picture of a glass sitting on driftwood.  This happens because the viewer has no reference point on what the material is or background was.', '2004-06-25 03:07:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(779050, 84146, 20539, '<td valign="top">the colour of the strawberries is not sharp enough. if they were a vivid red, it would be a good thing to highlight them.</td>', 'the colour of the strawberries is not sharp enough. if they were a vivid red, it would be a good thing to highlight them.', '2004-06-25 03:11:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(779051, 84283, 20539, '<td valign="top">very nice poses.</td>', 'very nice poses.', '2004-06-25 03:11:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(779052, 84339, 20539, '<td valign="top">ver y sharp image. this makes it good! - 8</td>', 'ver y sharp image. this makes it good! - 8', '2004-06-25 03:12:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(779053, 84266, 20539, '<td valign="top">excellent dof. nice shot and desaturation. 9</td>', 'excellent dof. nice shot and desaturation. 9', '2004-06-25 03:13:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(779054, 84689, 14355, '<td valign="top">I would have voted this a ten if just the tree was in color............. with the grass and small circle of rocks at the bottom in color too.  Having  the grass desaturated,  the cloud shadows on the left would have given it a dynamite amount of contrast and balanced the entire picture to perfection.  With one or two of the lone rocks on the left side left in color it would have been a spectacular picture.</td>', 'I would have voted this a ten if just the tree was in color............. with the grass and small circle of rocks at the bottom in color too.  Having  the grass desaturated,  the cloud shadows on the left would have given it a dynamite amount of contrast and balanced the entire picture to perfection.  With one or two of the lone rocks on the left side left in color it would have been a spectacular picture.', '2004-06-25 03:13:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(779059, 84820, 14355, '<td valign="top">You know how much I like this picture.......... it might look fine  because you know the people in the picture and what the original looked like.  Probably the first time you''ve seen these guys actually working.  But to a viewer it lacks a subject to focus on - one guy bending over a hole, one guy working on machinery, two guys stuffing a black something that is cropped out.  If they had at least turned to face the camera and waved while you said, "Cheese!" it would have been kinda cool in a campy way.  What might have worked on this picture - leave the background and desaturated the workers -  would have  made a statement about how people view manual laborers as not there...... and a better picture as well.</td>', 'You know how much I like this picture.......... it might look fine  because you know the people in the picture and what the original looked like.  Probably the first time you''ve seen these guys actually working.  But to a viewer it lacks a subject to focus on - one guy bending over a hole, one guy working on machinery, two guys stuffing a black something that is cropped out.  If they had at least turned to face the camera and waved while you said, "Cheese!" it would have been kinda cool in a campy way.  What might have worked on this picture - leave the background and desaturated the workers -  would have  made a statement about how people view manual laborers as not there...... and a better picture as well.', '2004-06-25 03:23:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(779064, 84901, 14355, '<td valign="top">I''ve come back to this picture three times and it still looks like a normal picture to me.  It''s a nice enough picture with great colors and a fine focus but there is absolutly nothing in the background or foreground - nothing is greyscaled. What were you thinking??</td>', 'I''ve come back to this picture three times and it still looks like a normal picture to me.  It''s a nice enough picture with great colors and a fine focus but there is absolutly nothing in the background or foreground - nothing is greyscaled. What were you thinking??', '2004-06-25 03:30:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(779069, 84840, 14355, '<td valign="top">Even on a second visit to this picture -  it ooks like a normal picture of flowers growing in a rock on a cloudy day.   The flowers at the bottom being the main subject, it''s not until the eye wanders up the trail away from the subject and discovers the sky and trees are black and white.  Desaturating this picture doesn''t enhance the main subject...... it just makes the picture a curiosity.  A closer crop on the flowers would have given you the rock''s texture for contrast, the greens to desaturate and the blooms would have make the picture stand out.</td>', 'Even on a second visit to this picture -  it ooks like a normal picture of flowers growing in a rock on a cloudy day.   The flowers at the bottom being the main subject, it''s not until the eye wanders up the trail away from the subject and discovers the sky and trees are black and white.  Desaturating this picture doesn''t enhance the main subject...... it just makes the picture a curiosity.  A closer crop on the flowers would have given you the rock''s texture for contrast, the greens to desaturate and the blooms would have make the picture stand out.', '2004-06-25 03:35:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(779070, 84680, 6804, '<td valign="top">Excellent Entry!  This is fun for the eye to browse around all the action. Clean, clear detail and the umbrellas bring flavor to the scene.  My only thought on how I might improve on this would be to take a look at how bright the shirt is on the guy at the bottom right. I might try to tone his shirt down to blend with the rest of the people.    I like this.  9</td>', 'Excellent Entry!  This is fun for the eye to browse around all the action. Clean, clear detail and the umbrellas bring flavor to the scene.  My only thought on how I might improve on this would be to take a look at how bright the shirt is on the guy at the bottom right. I might try to tone his shirt down to blend with the rest of the people.    I like this.  9', '2004-06-25 03:35:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(779080, 84334, 14355, '<td valign="top">I keep comming back to this picture - it''s like a train wreck in progress, you want to look aways but can''t.......... It''s just wrong in so many ways it slowly becomes right.   There are questions that must be asked, like why, in Gods name, would you want the viewer to focus on parts of dead phone poles and a shrub when you have a neat rainbow in the picture?  What were you thinking?  And why are you peeking through dead poles when you should be looking for a better positon to catch the rainbow?  Hey, I have the answer - you were thinking it would make allot of people come back  to see it ''cause it''s so unusual....... and it worked.  This picture grows on you in an abstract way - so I am going to rate it high.  Good luck.</td>', 'I keep comming back to this picture - it''s like a train wreck in progress, you want to look aways but can''t.......... It''s just wrong in so many ways it slowly becomes right.   There are questions that must be asked, like why, in Gods name, would you want the viewer to focus on parts of dead phone poles and a shrub when you have a neat rainbow in the picture?  What were you thinking?  And why are you peeking through dead poles when you should be looking for a better positon to catch the rainbow?  Hey, I have the answer - you were thinking it would make allot of people come back  to see it ''cause it''s so unusual....... and it worked.  This picture grows on you in an abstract way - so I am going to rate it high.  Good luck.', '2004-06-25 03:45:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(779082, 83785, 14355, '<td valign="top">If a picture of a hole is boreing in color, what makes you think it looks better with most of the color  missing??   I sure hope you do better in your other hobbies.</td>', 'If a picture of a hole is boreing in color, what makes you think it looks better with most of the color  missing??   I sure hope you do better in your other hobbies.', '2004-06-25 03:46:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(779085, 84904, 14355, '<td valign="top">On revisit - it''s a well taken shot - just confusing with two main subjects.  I would  have chosen between the model and the motorcycle to desaturate.  I think the whole thing in color with the model desat would have made a good composition or vice versa.  The bike has too many greyscale colors to make a good desat object.  Excellent workmanship isolating the color areas from the backgound.  Great job.</td>', 'On revisit - it''s a well taken shot - just confusing with two main subjects.  I would  have chosen between the model and the motorcycle to desaturate.  I think the whole thing in color with the model desat would have made a good composition or vice versa.  The bike has too many greyscale colors to make a good desat object.  Excellent workmanship isolating the color areas from the backgound.  Great job.', '2004-06-25 03:51:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(779087, 84382, 6804, '<td valign="top">This is a great example of desaturation so I give you high marks for meeting the challenge. I like the overall picture here and if I knew this guy I would hang this on my wall.  I think when selecting a photograph to apply the desaturation technique, I would find an area of the picture to enhance the main subject rather than to have the only color in the shot drawing my attention away from the main subject. (just my preference) but nice work all the same.</td>', 'This is a great example of desaturation so I give you high marks for meeting the challenge. I like the overall picture here and if I knew this guy I would hang this on my wall.  I think when selecting a photograph to apply the desaturation technique, I would find an area of the picture to enhance the main subject rather than to have the only color in the shot drawing my attention away from the main subject. (just my preference) but nice work all the same.', '2004-06-25 03:52:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(779094, 84753, 14355, '<td valign="top">You know how much I just love this picture.  It''s a great subject, good focus, excellent dof.  You would have been better off leaving the original background in place - your use of the burn tool did not eleminate it - there are shades of dark and light all over.  Your picture has five main parts - hand, pitcher, milk, glass, and pie.  The metal fork and white milk represent already greyscalled items.  The hand and glass are composed of colors and shades people already understand and are the best objects to desaturate.  Nobody knows what kind of pie or color the pitcher is - so these are the  two subjects to consider highlighting and becoming your main subject.  Because you selected the milk instead of the pie or pitcher -  all you accomplished was coverting a color picture to black and white.  I would have cropped this picture halfway through the pitcher and desaturated everything but the pie and the pitcher half to balance it</td>', 'You know how much I just love this picture.  It''s a great subject, good focus, excellent dof.  You would have been better off leaving the original background in place - your use of the burn tool did not eleminate it - there are shades of dark and light all over.  Your picture has five main parts - hand, pitcher, milk, glass, and pie.  The metal fork and white milk represent already greyscalled items.  The hand and glass are composed of colors and shades people already understand and are the best objects to desaturate.  Nobody knows what kind of pie or color the pitcher is - so these are the  two subjects to consider highlighting and becoming your main subject.  Because you selected the milk instead of the pie or pitcher -  all you accomplished was coverting a color picture to black and white.  I would have cropped this picture halfway through the pitcher and desaturated everything but the pie and the pitcher half to balance it', '2004-06-25 04:12:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(779106, 84923, 14355, '<td valign="top">Although it''s well focus and has a nice dof there is too much negative space on the top.  Cropping 15% off the top would help.  The glass, diamonds, and pearls are normally close to greyscale shades.  Having them desaturated does not enhance  the picture......... they are not really good objects to have front and center in a desaturation challenge.   The beads have a pleasing natural color to them and stand out, but, it doesn''t continue into the glass wich woud have made this picture.</td>', 'Although it''s well focus and has a nice dof there is too much negative space on the top.  Cropping 15% off the top would help.  The glass, diamonds, and pearls are normally close to greyscale shades.  Having them desaturated does not enhance  the picture......... they are not really good objects to have front and center in a desaturation challenge.   The beads have a pleasing natural color to them and stand out, but, it doesn''t continue into the glass wich woud have made this picture.', '2004-06-25 04:29:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(779111, 84650, 9668, '<td valign="top">Great capture of the expression on the dog''s face.  I notice that one eye is brown and the other one is a bit darker, so I can''t really tell iff it is totally in color. Too bad about clipping off the top of it''s ear. I would like more of an even crop: with both ears distance from the edge the same. I love black labs (have one myself), thier eyes can just say it all. Nice job.</td>', 'Great capture of the expression on the dog''s face.  I notice that one eye is brown and the other one is a bit darker, so I can''t really tell iff it is totally in color. Too bad about clipping off the top of it''s ear. I would like more of an even crop: with both ears distance from the edge the same. I love black labs (have one myself), thier eyes can just say it all. Nice job.', '2004-06-25 04:34:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(779114, 84512, 14355, '<td valign="top">This was not a good choice of picture to use for this challenge.  Water and foam spray are generally a greyscale colored item in many pictures.  Here it occupies 90% of the image and greyscaling is not noticed.  The person is already the main subject - nothing else is in competition with him for that -  leaving all the colors on the board, clothing, face, hands, and chute hardware  make this picture look like a normal picture.  The greyscaled trees in the far background add nothing to the shot..... just makes it look cloudy over there.</td>', 'This was not a good choice of picture to use for this challenge.  Water and foam spray are generally a greyscale colored item in many pictures.  Here it occupies 90% of the image and greyscaling is not noticed.  The person is already the main subject - nothing else is in competition with him for that -  leaving all the colors on the board, clothing, face, hands, and chute hardware  make this picture look like a normal picture.  The greyscaled trees in the far background add nothing to the shot..... just makes it look cloudy over there.', '2004-06-25 04:39:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(779116, 84608, 6804, '<td valign="top">I love the richness of this. The bold blue brings a modern feel to the old style architecture.  You''ve got a good eye to be able to see these elements as a pleasing photograph with the intention of desaturating like this. Bravo!!!  10</td>', 'I love the richness of this. The bold blue brings a modern feel to the old style architecture.  You''ve got a good eye to be able to see these elements as a pleasing photograph with the intention of desaturating like this. Bravo!!!  10', '2004-06-25 04:43:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(779117, 84912, 14355, '<td valign="top">This is a really nice, simple, well composed shot.  Great dof and a very pleasant soft focus to it.  The way the flower stands out is perfect.  The yellow eys - they look un natural, alien, and totally out of place.  Even if they are that color in real life, I woud have greyscaled them with the rest of the face.  This picture would have earned a 9 or 10 from everyone easy.</td>', 'This is a really nice, simple, well composed shot.  Great dof and a very pleasant soft focus to it.  The way the flower stands out is perfect.  The yellow eys - they look un natural, alien, and totally out of place.  Even if they are that color in real life, I woud have greyscaled them with the rest of the face.  This picture would have earned a 9 or 10 from everyone easy.', '2004-06-25 04:44:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(779118, 83771, 14355, '<td valign="top">Nothing for the viewer to identify with and realize what colors are missing.   In this pic - I can''t tell what you desaturated.</td>', 'Nothing for the viewer to identify with and realize what colors are missing.   In this pic - I can''t tell what you desaturated.', '2004-06-25 04:44:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(779119, 84283, 14355, '<td valign="top">It''s a very neat picture with a sharp focus, I like how the water looks.  There are too many faded colors and allot of unknown itmes for the desaturation effect to be recognized.  It looks like a normal picture with all the colors desaturated.</td>', 'It''s a very neat picture with a sharp focus, I like how the water looks.  There are too many faded colors and allot of unknown itmes for the desaturation effect to be recognized.  It looks like a normal picture with all the colors desaturated.', '2004-06-25 04:49:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(779122, 84204, 9668, '<td valign="top">Intersting choice to desatures, does make it stand out but I wonder what not the entire instrument is not saturated. Background is also a bit distracting</td>', 'Intersting choice to desatures, does make it stand out but I wonder what not the entire instrument is not saturated. Background is also a bit distracting', '2004-06-25 04:54:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(779127, 84717, 9668, '<td valign="top">The lighting on the front of the machine are very distracting. My eye whats to follow the light patterns instead of focus on the logo. Good focus</td>', 'The lighting on the front of the machine are very distracting. My eye whats to follow the light patterns instead of focus on the logo. Good focus', '2004-06-25 04:56:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(779133, 84744, 9668, '<td valign="top">This must of been a bit of work to desaturate! Nice subject choice, desaturation really makes sense.</td>', 'This must of been a bit of work to desaturate! Nice subject choice, desaturation really makes sense.', '2004-06-25 05:21:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(779142, 84207, 9668, '<td valign="top">I would like to see her more in focus AND in color. Other wise the focal point is out of focus. Cute little model =).</td>', 'I would like to see her more in focus AND in color. Other wise the focal point is out of focus. Cute little model =).', '2004-06-25 05:38:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(779147, 84826, 9668, '<td valign="top">Great focus! Although I wouldn''t seeing more of the pillar blurred, but that is minor. Nice coloration, good capture.</td>', 'Great focus! Although I wouldn''t seeing more of the pillar blurred, but that is minor. Nice coloration, good capture.', '2004-06-25 05:43:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(779164, 84065, 16004, '<td valign="top">This is wonderful subject matter for a challenge of this type.  the car is gorgeous, and the blue shades are nice and bright and bold.  Though chrome also looks very lovely, with the complimentary deep blue sky reflected in the top half of the bumper and the hub caps.  only minor criticisms include that i think it might be prefereable if the background visible through the windows had been desatted, if you had cloned out your reflection clearly evident in the front corner, and most importantly, the car should really have been in motion.  it looks just a bit odd (to my pre-conceived expectation) being situated on a nice picturesque straight road, but stationary.  a very slight motion blur to the road surface would have helped, methinks.    i might be wrong, it might have been in motion - it just to me, it doesnt really convey that.  Overall though its a very lovely poster-friendly image, gets a 7 from me and I hope it does well.</td>', 'This is wonderful subject matter for a challenge of this type.  the car is gorgeous, and the blue shades are nice and bright and bold.  Though chrome also looks very lovely, with the complimentary deep blue sky reflected in the top half of the bumper and the hub caps.  only minor criticisms include that i think it might be prefereable if the background visible through the windows had been desatted, if you had cloned out your reflection clearly evident in the front corner, and most importantly, the car should really have been in motion.  it looks just a bit odd (to my pre-conceived expectation) being situated on a nice picturesque straight road, but stationary.  a very slight motion blur to the road surface would have helped, methinks.    i might be wrong, it might have been in motion - it just to me, it doesnt really convey that.  Overall though its a very lovely poster-friendly image, gets a 7 from me and I hope it does well.', '2004-06-25 06:11:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(779170, 84864, 15002, '<td valign="top">nice pic.  removeing the remaining color from right wing and aroung antenae would make better</td>', 'nice pic.  removeing the remaining color from right wing and aroung antenae would make better', '2004-06-25 06:20:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(779172, 84861, 15002, '<td valign="top">contrast within the iris is great, yellow is good.  the contrast beteen iriis and background could be improved</td>', 'contrast within the iris is great, yellow is good.  the contrast beteen iriis and background could be improved', '2004-06-25 06:23:41.000000', NULL, 1);
