(782716, 84282, 18349, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the top tenner, Julia!!  It''s great...such power and the desat is perfect.  Love it; added it to my faves!!!! :o)</td>', 'Congrats on the top tenner, Julia!!  It''s great...such power and the desat is perfect.  Love it; added it to my faves!!!! :o)', '2004-06-28 12:50:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(782718, 84769, 7291, '<td valign="top">I knew this was one of the better pics in this challenge.  I''m just wondering how you accomplished such a deep DOF with f2.8.  Very cool and congrats.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-06-28 15:48:19.</i></td>', 'I knew this was one of the better pics in this challenge.  I''m just wondering how you accomplished such a deep DOF with f2.8.  Very cool and congrats.', '2004-06-28 12:50:00.000000', '2004-06-28 16:48:19.000000', 0),
(782719, 84339, 18349, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your top five finish...this is a very nice shot and the desat is perfect.  Wonderful!!!  :o)</td>', 'Congratulations on your top five finish...this is a very nice shot and the desat is perfect.  Wonderful!!!  :o)', '2004-06-28 12:50:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(782763, 84550, 18349, '<td valign="top">I was quite surprised to find this one at 91st instead of in the top ten...it''s a great shot.  I get my little mannequin this week and I''m so excited about it!  You did such a great job with this one.  Don''t be discouraged at all!!!!  :o)</td>', 'I was quite surprised to find this one at 91st instead of in the top ten...it''s a great shot.  I get my little mannequin this week and I''m so excited about it!  You did such a great job with this one.  Don''t be discouraged at all!!!!  :o)', '2004-06-28 13:09:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(782797, 84769, 14603, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by K-Rob:</b></div><hr/><i> I knew this was one of the better pics in this challenge.  I''m just wondering how you accomplished such a deep DOF with f2.8.  Very cool and conrats. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I puzzled over that very same thing when I submitted the image.It`s there in black and white(no pun intended) on the exif data and I thought I was misreading it..I can only assume that the deep DOF is a bit of an optical illusion owing to the type of landscape showing through the window<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-06-29 05:12:32.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by K-Rob: I knew this was one of the better pics in this challenge.  I''m just wondering how you accomplished such a deep DOF with f2.8.  Very cool and conrats.   I puzzled over that very same thing when I submitted the image.It`s there in black and white(no pun intended) on the exif data and I thought I was misreading it..I can only assume that the deep DOF is a bit of an optical illusion owing to the type of landscape showing through the window', '2004-06-28 13:24:20.000000', '2004-06-29 06:12:32.000000', 0),
(782819, 84354, 7350, '<td valign="top">I''m shocked to see this one so low.  Many commenters seem to think that you didn''t notice the grain, or that it is there on accident.  I think it would be difficult to get this much grain in your camera on accident - it is very obviously done on purpose, and I find it to be very effective.  One commenter mentioned that perhaps you could have left the grain out of the umbrella, and put it in everywhere else.  That is an interesting idea that might have worked as well.  At any rate, I think this is a fantastic shot, with a wonderful mood.  Nice contrast in the B/W areas, and great idea.</td>', 'I''m shocked to see this one so low.  Many commenters seem to think that you didn''t notice the grain, or that it is there on accident.  I think it would be difficult to get this much grain in your camera on accident - it is very obviously done on purpose, and I find it to be very effective.  One commenter mentioned that perhaps you could have left the grain out of the umbrella, and put it in everywhere else.  That is an interesting idea that might have worked as well.  At any rate, I think this is a fantastic shot, with a wonderful mood.  Nice contrast in the B/W areas, and great idea.', '2004-06-28 13:33:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(782833, 84871, 472, '<td valign="top">thanks for the comments : ) &gt;.  i hadnt entered in a while but i had something that fit.   i enjoyed this shoot.</td>', 'thanks for the comments : ) >.  i hadnt entered in a while but i had something that fit.   i enjoyed this shoot.', '2004-06-28 13:41:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(782857, 84383, 19708, '<td valign="top">Congrats David,<br/> <br/>As a "car guy", I found this one was exceptional. Definitely has an advertisement feel &amp; quality to it! One of my favorites.<br/> <br/>Well Done!</td>', 'Congrats David, As a "car guy", I found this one was exceptional. Definitely has an advertisement feel & quality to it! One of my favorites. Well Done!', '2004-06-28 14:00:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(782861, 84930, 19708, '<td valign="top">Congrats Eddy,<br/> <br/>My hat is off to you for a first-ever attempt, no wait, it was an effect job of selective desauration, not an attempt. This was a stunning shot and so well-suited to the challenge.<br/> <br/>Well Done!</td>', 'Congrats Eddy, My hat is off to you for a first-ever attempt, no wait, it was an effect job of selective desauration, not an attempt. This was a stunning shot and so well-suited to the challenge. Well Done!', '2004-06-28 14:04:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(782871, 84889, 11467, '<td valign="top">Most impressive!<br/>Even more impressive to think it is a self portrate taken with a remote!!<br/>Where is the remote??<br/></td>', 'Most impressive!Even more impressive to think it is a self portrate taken with a remote!!Where is the remote??', '2004-06-28 14:14:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(782873, 84354, 714, '<td valign="top">thanks, Steve!  <br/> <br/>I tried the grain like you mentioned but it looked as though the umbrella was fake.  I should have submited the one without grain.  Oh well, a lesson I will never learn.  Creativity burns in my soul. :-)</td>', 'thanks, Steve!   I tried the grain like you mentioned but it looked as though the umbrella was fake.  I should have submited the one without grain.  Oh well, a lesson I will never learn.  Creativity burns in my soul. :-)', '2004-06-28 14:17:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(782875, 84556, 4482, '<td valign="top">Great choice of desaturation! Love this shot! great work!<br/> <br/>Yanik</td>', 'Great choice of desaturation! Love this shot! great work! Yanik', '2004-06-28 14:22:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(782876, 84871, 669, '<td valign="top">Surprised this wasn''t top ten.  I didn''t vote on Selective Desat, but I saw this shot and thought it had a certain ''sheen'' of quality.  I knew I recognised the quality and style but I failed to work out who it was!<br/> <br/>Very nice work, as always.  Again, think it should have come higher.</td>', 'Surprised this wasn''t top ten.  I didn''t vote on Selective Desat, but I saw this shot and thought it had a certain ''sheen'' of quality.  I knew I recognised the quality and style but I failed to work out who it was! Very nice work, as always.  Again, think it should have come higher.', '2004-06-28 14:22:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(782877, 84485, 5112, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, Laurie, this is a wonderful image!  And congratulations on your very first ribbon (may you get many more).<br/></td>', 'Congratulations, Laurie, this is a wonderful image!  And congratulations on your very first ribbon (may you get many more).', '2004-06-28 14:22:57.000000', NULL, 0),
